6TH ASCENSION GAME SUMMARY ("Better Strength Through Tinning")

Madusk the Filcher      St:18/76 Dx:20 Co:18 In:18 Wi:18 Ch:14  Chaotic
Astral Plane $:0  HP:274(274) Pw:128(165) AC:-37 Xp:25/50014404 T:52743

Conducts: wishless, polyselfless, polyitemless

This was my second rogue ascension, this one with some conducts. I think
I've gotten the "feel" of the role now. I enjoy playing petless chaotic
rogue with Stormbringer, and (as with wizard, my favorite role) I enjoy
dagger machinegunning. This was the first game I found and used a tinning
kit, which is heavy but adds some fun (strength, intrinsics, etc.).

Getting down to, and through, Sokoban was tricky because I hardly found
any armor (was only AC:5 by the end of the Zoo). Then I did the shortest
town/luckstone path I could, and waited until later when I had [oMR to
fully clean out the Mines. I managed to avoid hitting ^poly this time
(took me 4 games to keep polyselfless conduct through this phase).

Once I did find [oMR and fully cleaned out the Mines, it was a bonanza,
including a marker and conflict ring; from there it was all downhill.
The wishless and polyitemless conducts don't mean as much when the RNG
supplies everything anyway. :-)

[Screen shot and final stats are at the bottom, after the game timeline
and "lessons learned" (my running notes during the game)]


